From f260d2925fc75dbe4d1099597b113324bb598cc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:50:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rc: one shared AiMesh node list for Gatekeeper, the rules
 engine, Policy Routing and rwatch (102.8 line)

AiMesh nodes are infrastructure, not clients. Gatekeeper has exempted them since v2.7.3 and was
the only surface that did: the rules engine (Service Intercept rewrites a service for every LAN
source, and a node is a LAN source) and Policy Routing carried no exemption, so one broad rule
could cut a node off.
- rc/reaper_aimesh.c (new): reaper_aimesh_macs(), Gatekeeper's cfg_relist parser moved unchanged
  (a host harness ran the old and the new gk_emit_relist on six fixtures: byte-identical output;
  the over-cap log is now one summary line), and the applet reaper_aimesh_sync, which refreshes
  the hash:mac set reaper_aimesh by staging and swap under a file lock (/sbin link, rc.c applet
  table, rc.h externs with REAPER_AIMESH_SET / REAPER_AIMESH_MAX 64, rc/Makefile OBJS).
- gatekeeper.c uses the shared parser and syncs the set. reaper_fw.c syncs and creates it when
  the rules run and returns AiMesh sources at the top of REAPER_FWI / REAPER_FWF (after the head)
  and in nat REAPER_FWN, IPv4 and IPv6. reaper_pbr.c returns them after the REPLY return. rwatch
  refreshes the set on each tick.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
